From b9395674f91cfcfb8439a3cab5dfba4b6481b177 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grizbeard <justin.morken@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 23:51:15 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 04/11] Route the library tree-item icons through the skin
 override too

The skin override only reached icons a LibraryFeature builds for itself.
Five sidebar icons are set on tree items instead, straight from the Qt
resource, so they kept the built-in orange while the feature rows above
them followed the skin: the Crates node under Auto DJ, Serato's crates,
the current history session, and the padlocks on a locked playlist or
crate.

Lift the lookup out of the constructor into LibraryFeature::iconForName
and call it from those five, so a tree item and the feature it sits under
resolve their icons the same way -- and so the QIcon::Selected
registration that stops Qt tinting a highlighted row applies to them as
well. Serato parses its crates on a worker thread through a free
function, so that one takes the icon as an argument, built once on the
GUI thread rather than per crate.

Three of the names had no override to find, so add ic_library_locked,
ic_library_locked_tracklist and ic_library_history_current to the set the
Terminal generator emits.

Verified in the running app: no saturated orange left anywhere in the
sidebar, with Auto DJ and History expanded. The two padlocks need a
locked playlist to appear and were not exercised.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
